00:47:49,840 --> 00:47:54,680
 I think 10% of the founders that we've talked to

1045
00:47:54,680 --> 00:47:58,520
 and looked at are building social related projects.

1046
00:47:58,520 --> 00:48:00,880
 So I think people see this opportunity

1047
00:48:00,880 --> 00:48:02,960
 and they expect that it's gonna be a thing

1048
00:48:02,960 --> 00:48:05,280
 given how big it was in web too.

1049
00:48:05,280 --> 00:48:06,760
 - Yeah, then there's prediction markets.

1050
00:48:06,760 --> 00:48:09,400
 Of course, those have been huge this year.

1051
00:48:09,400 --> 00:48:12,680
 No surprise given the incredible dynamics

1052
00:48:12,680 --> 00:48:15,680
 and volatility related to the election.

1053
00:48:15,680 --> 00:48:17,520
 - Yeah, prediction markets is an idea

1054
00:48:17,520 --> 00:48:19,840
 that people have been talking about for decades,

1055
00:48:19,840 --> 00:48:21,640
 but have been hamstrung.

1056
00:48:21,640 --> 00:48:26,160
 And people are actually coming around to their value.

1057
00:48:26,160 --> 00:48:29,280
 An ability to source up knowledge

1058
00:48:29,280 --> 00:48:31,920
 from disparate parts of the world

1059
00:48:31,920 --> 00:48:35,320
 and kind of get a better, more informed picture

1060
00:48:35,320 --> 00:48:36,240
 of the state of the world

1061
00:48:36,240 --> 00:48:38,680
 and how things might shake out.

1062
00:48:38,680 --> 00:48:41,040
 It's interesting to see that it's actually finally

1063
00:48:41,040 --> 00:48:43,760
 getting some traction when it's a very old idea

1064
00:48:43,760 --> 00:48:46,640
 that has been stalled for so long.

1065
00:48:46,640 --> 00:48:48,520
 All right, Eddie, we've been putting out reports

1066
00:48:48,520 --> 00:48:49,920
 for three years.

1067
00:48:49,920 --> 00:48:53,520
 What's been most surprising looking at this year's report

1068
00:48:53,520 --> 00:48:55,880
 compared to earlier reports?

1069
00:48:55,880 --> 00:49:00,240
 - I don't know, stepping back, I'd say,

1070
00:49:00,240 --> 00:49:02,720
 when we're deep in the mix, like we are,

1071
00:49:02,720 --> 00:49:06,240
 it often feels like nothing is coming fast enough.

1072
00:49:06,240 --> 00:49:07,520
 I feel that all the time.

1073
00:49:07,520 --> 00:49:11,220
 I want it right now, right now, I'm sick of waiting.

1074
00:49:11,220 --> 00:49:15,320
 And there are some areas that have definitely lagged,

1075
00:49:15,320 --> 00:49:19,840
 but at the same time, it is a little bit unbelievable

1076
00:49:19,840 --> 00:49:22,200
 when you look back at the progress.

1077
00:49:22,200 --> 00:49:24,480
 Let's be very conservative in our estimates

1078
00:49:24,480 --> 00:49:26,760
 and let's say we have 30 million monthly

1079
00:49:26,760 --> 00:49:29,400
 active users of blockchains.

1080
00:49:29,400 --> 00:49:31,440
 That's pretty damn good.

1081
00:49:31,440 --> 00:49:34,000
 Like I'm pretty happy with where that is

1082
00:49:34,000 --> 00:49:37,160
 given the historical infrastructure limits.

1083
00:49:37,160 --> 00:49:40,720
 Like about a year ago, we were all debating

1084
00:49:40,720 --> 00:49:43,960
 how long it would take things to start to heat up

1085
00:49:43,960 --> 00:49:46,880
 in terms of on-chain usage.

1086
00:49:46,880 --> 00:49:51,120
 And where I ended up was that six months after Denkoon,

1087
00:49:51,120 --> 00:49:54,960
 six months after '48, '44, is when we'd start to see

1088
00:49:54,960 --> 00:49:57,080
 like new types of stories

1089
00:49:57,080 --> 00:49:59,560
 because that's about how long it takes.

1090
00:49:59,560 --> 00:50:03,760
 And we're just like six months after.

1091
00:50:03,760 --> 00:50:05,920
 And I think that that's exactly what's happening.

1092
00:50:05,920 --> 00:50:08,680
 Like I think the payments thing is one of those things.

1093
00:50:08,680 --> 00:50:10,200
 And I think some of these new networks,

1094
00:50:10,200 --> 00:50:13,680
 some of these like deep in networks are examples of that.

1095
00:50:13,680 --> 00:50:17,440
 So it feels very on track to me and I'm very pleased with that.

1096
00:50:17,440 --> 00:50:20,000
 That's kind of surprising, maybe in a certain way.

1097
00:50:20,000 --> 00:50:23,840
 That is surprising to me that it feels very kind of like

1098
00:50:23,840 --> 00:50:26,880
 we are thinking it's going unfold.

1099
00:50:26,880 --> 00:50:31,440
 If you had to cast your prediction a year ahead,

1100
00:50:31,440 --> 00:50:32,800
 what do you think is going to be the theme

1101
00:50:32,800 --> 00:50:35,160
 of State of crypto 2025?

1102
00:50:35,160 --> 00:50:37,840
 - I hope that all the extra block space is filled

1103
00:50:37,840 --> 00:50:40,760
 with something, something productive.

1104
00:50:40,760 --> 00:50:41,760
 That's what I hope it's about.

1105
00:50:41,760 --> 00:50:43,880
 It's about what fills that block space.

1106
00:50:43,880 --> 00:50:47,280
 We just started creating all these L2s and new block chains.

1107
00:50:47,280 --> 00:50:50,320
 And maybe something that we didn't put in the report

1108
00:50:50,320 --> 00:50:52,480
 'cause it can be challenging to present

1109
00:50:52,480 --> 00:50:53,680
 in a very straightforward way.

1110
00:50:53,680 --> 00:50:56,560
 But bridges are great for people in crypto.

1111
00:50:56,560 --> 00:50:58,640
 You know that three years ago,

1112
00:50:58,640 --> 00:51:00,680
 there were very few bridges and they were terrible

1113
00:51:00,680 --> 00:51:02,560
 and they were slow and they were expensive

1114
00:51:02,560 --> 00:51:04,200
 and they were error prone.

1115
00:51:04,200 --> 00:51:06,440
 There's just a lot wrong with them.

1116
00:51:06,440 --> 00:51:09,560
 Now bridges, there's myriad options,

1117
00:51:09,560 --> 00:51:13,120
 really high quality, fast, super affordable,

1118
00:51:13,120 --> 00:51:14,640
 great connectivity.

1119
00:51:14,640 --> 00:51:16,680
 That's like no question.

1120
00:51:16,680 --> 00:51:19,120
 Anyone in crypto would agree with that.

1121
00:51:19,120 --> 00:51:20,600
 Well, now that we have good bridges

1122
00:51:20,600 --> 00:51:21,760
 and now we have good L2s,

1123
00:51:21,760 --> 00:51:24,320
 we're getting tons more L2s and tons more bridges

1124
00:51:24,320 --> 00:51:28,240
 and tons more interoperability questions and fragmentation.

1125
00:51:28,240 --> 00:51:30,440
 So as always happens with technology,

1126
00:51:30,440 --> 00:51:33,160
 you solve one problem, you create another.

1127
00:51:33,160 --> 00:51:35,320
 I'm beginning to see signs

1128
00:51:35,320 --> 00:51:38,280
 that there are really, really great strategies

1129
00:51:38,280 --> 00:51:41,400
 to solve interoperability.

1130
00:51:41,400 --> 00:51:44,640
 And so I hope the combination of good interoperability

1131
00:51:44,640 --> 00:51:49,560
 plus good block space means finally great user experience

1132
00:51:49,560 --> 00:51:52,400
 for a family of applications.

1133
00:51:52,400 --> 00:51:54,640
 If that was the case at the end of 2025,

1134
00:51:54,640 --> 00:51:56,960
 I would be really pleased.

1135
00:51:56,960 --> 00:51:58,800
 That's great for the wishlist.

1136
00:51:58,800 --> 00:52:01,200
 I really hope that in the coming years,

1137
00:52:01,200 --> 00:52:04,000
 our section on infrastructure gets smaller

1138
00:52:04,000 --> 00:52:06,520
 and our section on applications gets bigger.

1139
00:52:06,520 --> 00:52:08,800
 I think there's still a place to report

1140
00:52:08,800 --> 00:52:10,520
 on key infrastructure developments,

1141
00:52:10,520 --> 00:52:13,400
 which I think will continue to happen over the coming years,

1142
00:52:13,400 --> 00:52:15,880
 but I think it should be hopefully more

1143
00:52:15,880 --> 00:52:19,880
 about how do we just overall improve the user experience.

1144
00:52:19,880 --> 00:52:23,200
 There's account abstraction protocols, interoperability,

1145
00:52:23,200 --> 00:52:26,000
 various developments that we can report on,

1146
00:52:26,000 --> 00:52:28,760
 but I hope that that does not be main story.

1147
00:52:28,760 --> 00:52:32,200
 I hope the main story of 2025 and the years following

1148
00:52:32,200 --> 00:52:35,680
 is that we now have a new set of applications

1149
00:52:35,680 --> 00:52:39,040
 that are proving to be real use cases

1150
00:52:39,040 --> 00:52:42,240
 for this technology that is attracting people.

1151
00:52:42,240 --> 00:52:45,680
 And so that is my hope for the years to come.

1152
00:52:45,680 --> 00:52:47,680
 We've made a lot of progress on infrastructure,

1153
00:52:47,680 --> 00:52:51,360
 but hopefully from here going forward,

1154
00:52:51,360 --> 00:52:53,880
 the improvements are more on the margin.

1155
00:52:53,880 --> 00:52:55,120
 Maybe in the years ahead,

1156
00:52:55,120 --> 00:52:57,800
 there won't even be a need for a state of crypto report.

1157
00:52:57,800 --> 00:53:00,120
 We will all just be using these applications

1158
00:53:00,120 --> 00:53:02,880
 and won't even know that there's crypto on the back end.

1159
00:53:02,880 --> 00:53:03,920
 Could be.

1160
00:53:03,920 --> 00:53:06,720
 We'll have to wait to know for sure.

1161
00:53:06,720 --> 00:53:07,880
 Thank you both for joining.

1162
00:53:07,880 --> 00:53:08,840
 Thank you, Robert.

1163
00:53:08,840 --> 00:53:10,000
 Thank you, Robert.

1164
00:53:17,680 --> 00:53:20,260
 (upbeat music)

